(This bug was split off from #31058)

On a MacBook 6,1 with linux 2.6.36 (64bit) and an external TFT connected via a
displayport->DVI adapter a kernel OOPS can be triggered by player a video
full-screen on the external monitor.

It only happens if VLC's option "Accelerated video output (Overlay)" is
enabled.

Note that on the laptop's internal screen I *can* play full screen with that
option *enabled* and no OOPS happens. It only happens on the external display.

